{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1231788-tribal-membership-and-non-standard-pack-totems","id":1231788,"title":"Tribal membership and non standard pack totems.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-02T06:34:06-07:00","id":1231788,"title":"Tribal membership and non standard pack totems.","content":"If a pack takes a non kosher totem can it affect their tribal memberships? Like is it possible for a bale hound to remain a member of a tribe. What about less nefarious totems, like a pack that takes a Fae, an angel or a ghost (ancestor whorshipers) as a totem. For the sake of this argument let's assume this is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T07:13:48-07:00","id":1231800,"title":"","content":"I think it has been said that a Pack's Totem and Tribal Totem occupy different &quot;slots&quot; in a Werewolf's spiritual hierarchy. So, picking conflicting Totems is a good way to make life uncomfortable for the Uratha in question, but isn't against any rules, per se.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T08:15:56-07:00","id":1231814,"title":"","content":"Your firstborn is unlikely to directly revoke tribal status over your choice in pack totems. It's more about how the rest of your tribe treats you when they find out.<br /> <br /> That said, if you're openly taking a bale hound appropriate personal or pack totem, there may be a few wolves in your tribe who would like a word with you.<br /> <br /> Taking a Ghost as a totem would probably be difficult, since they're not the same as spirits, and werewolves normally can't interact with them, though I imagine some majority Bone Shadow packs do, and are generally seen as 'eccentric' by others. The fact that werewolves have ancestor spirits instead of ghosts means an ancestor totem is likely better received than a ghost, depending on who the ancestor was.<br /> <br /> Angels can vary wildly in form and function, and are usually programmed with a mission they're obsessively devoted to. The specifics of the mission will determine just how a tribe would react. If the mission is to flood a small town's silver mine, or maintain a series of bonfires by burning the correct books, it's probably more welcome than, say, nailing skinned homeless people to billboards.<br /> <br /> And of course, if your pack totem isn't up to party line, you could always try to hide it, shut up any pesky witnesses. Just a matter of how far you're willing to go to protect a secret.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 07-02-2018, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T18:50:10-07:00","id":1232012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1231788-tribal-membership-and-non-standard-pack-totems?p=1231814#post1231814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your firstborn is unlikely to directly revoke tribal status over your choice in pack totems. It's more about how the rest of your tribe treats you when they find out..</div> </div> </div> </div>This is mainly what I was wondering about. Can a pack's choice of totem be so offensive that the Firstborn kick them from their tribes. Sounds like for the most part the Firstborn don't really care what a pack does as long as they get their proper tribute. I reread part of Lore of the Forsaken today and that seems to be what that book says.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T20:49:59-07:00","id":1232038,"title":"","content":"If you take a Maeltinent totem, and start fucking with the Oath of the Moon for fun, it's not the Firstborn you'll have to worry about<b></b>: it's the tribes of the moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}